{"id": "EUVD-2026-93149", "enisaUuid": "1410d562-57ac-3886-9471-86633dde4797", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKEYS: trusted: Fix tpm2_load_cmd() boundary check\n\ntpm2_load_cmd() does boundary checks against the ASN.1 size i.e.,\npayload->blob_len. Address this by passing the decoded blob size to\ntpm2_load_cmd(), and use it for the boundary checks.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cc86227fea28aed86c1fb52a884560b4440da198", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b020b447338872440142fe8a57350a483da86b7a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3fd487c69ad3161e358c33c170bab0cf02a071b7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5afa57ea91481c6c49f194b0f5a5c4d96a4d7348", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9ddbc5f4bb498aff8096a5231574858a4bffee4f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/134825dfc971fbf2b1d0f58f0b3bce8332ad0afb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/114f00d738f15dd8c7318369edcdc53dd6d08763"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98221", "GHSA-ppw2-5gqj-39j4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "038a6a1c-286f-3138-ba45-bce1fb6dd852", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2219745250f388edacabe6cca73654131c67d0a <3fd487c69ad3161e358c33c170bab0cf02a071b7"}, {"id": "1c68688d-d5ab-3859-a5a7-a9ea712036af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2219745250f388edacabe6cca73654131c67d0a <9ddbc5f4bb498aff8096a5231574858a4bffee4f"}, {"id": "3af51a03-6a2e-36bb-a535-5e2248a1adb4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "42536f47-0f53-3b6e-855a-831bd7a7f7de", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.13"}, {"id": "78f1b35e-d105-387a-a477-e2cbd5cbf948", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1